      "reasons": [
        "The definition specifies that cooing involves producing “simple vocal sounds,” but the supplied packet only lists “stages in development include babbling, cooing, word imitation with cognition, and use of short sentences” and does not explicitly describe cooing as “simple” or characterise its vocal sounds.",
        "The rest of the definition aligns broadly with the packet’s general statement about “gradual expansion in complexity and meaning … through a maturational and learning process” and the stated developmental sequence (cooing before word imitation and short sentences), but the unsupported “simple vocal sounds” claim is substantive."
